['Here is the C code to generate three random integers, print them and their sums. The output will vary as it is based on the current time of the system clock which makes it different everytime you run it:

```C
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() 
{
    int a, b, c;

    srand( (unsigned)time(NULL) ); // initialize random seed

    /* generate three random numbers between 1001 and RAND_MAX */
    a = rand() % (RAND_MAX / 3 - 5) + 1001; 
    b = rand() % (2 *(RAND_MAX / 3) - 4 ) + 1001;  
    c = rand() % ( RAND_MAX - a - b) + 1001 ; // ensure that sum of three numbers won't exceed RAND_MAX

    printf("a: %d\n", a);
    printf("b: %d\n", b);
    printf("c: %d\n", c);
    printf("sum: %d\n", a + b + c );

    long long sum2 = (long long)a + b + c; // cast to a longer data type before addition
    printf("sum2: %lld\n", sum2);

    return 0;
}
```
This code first generates three random numbers between 1001 and RAND_MAX, ensuring that each is larger than 1000. The third number is generated to ensure that their sum won't exceed the maximum integer value of the system (RAND_MAX). Then it prints these three numbers and their sum, as well as the sum calculated using long long data type.
